& [OwnedProtocol]
  + NativeArtifactLifecycleBundle owns every supplied form from SOPSeed through ProducedUnverified ArtifactReceipt
  + NativeVerificationLifecycleBundle owns verifier plan observation receipt and optional complete second artifact lineage
  + NativeLifecycleValidationRequest selects artifact or verification replay explicitly and denies unknown fields and incomplete operation correspondence

& [CausalReplay]
  + validators run through envelope seed typed IR candidate plan native projection build plan capability sandbox approval trust authorization observation ledger and artifact receipt in exact dependency order
  + verification continues through plan optional whole second lineage observation and receipt
  + replay stops at the first fault and returns the deepest completed stage plus one typed bounded fault
  + passed failed and unresolved verification receipts are all valid representations when their exact derivations replay

& [MachineBoundary]
  + validate_native_lifecycle_json accepts one strict bounded UTF-8 JSON object and rejects empty malformed trailing unknown over-bound and wrong-operation inputs
  + cantor-compiler-lab reads stdin or one explicitly named file and emits one normalized JSON line
  + exit zero means coherent artifact or verification lineage exit one means semantic lifecycle refusal and exit two means wire or invocation refusal
  + no output path process spawn network clock environment import signing secret installation deployment artifact execution or successor recognition exists

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + response validity means internal coherence under caller-supplied public trust context only
  + fixed non-authority denies physical truth correctness safety verification passage permission globally atomic consumption and every later lifecycle authority
  + authorization's embedded approval must equal the separately supplied approval form
  + second-build evidence is never trusted without a complete independently replayed second ArtifactReceipt lineage

